      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In support of artists who put there whole soul into painstakingly piece by piece making avatars and worlds only for AI that has little effort put in it over half the time be pushed forward, I think this is a wonderful idea. Unsure of how enforcing this would go but it's better than the nothing we have right now. \n\nNeutrality or not we all gotta see the big picture, the future we want to see in vrc. Last year there was such a big uptick of AI generated \"Museums\" and \"Interactive worlds\" with little or nothing in them or just straight up stealing art and running through a generator. There is no effort put in these just laziness trying to pass as something it's not. \n\nIf there is it's actually got a human touch at least IN IT, not 100% AI.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
